menu "Diagnostics (subsys/diag)"

    config DIAG_MAX_WDT_TASKS
        int "Maximum tasks subscribed to the task watchdog through diag"
        default 8
        range 1 32
        help
            Size of the static table that records which tasks diag_task_register()
            subscribed, so diag_deinit() can unsubscribe exactly those. Deadline
            tasks (audio capture, USB device) are the intended subscribers.

    config DIAG_WDT_TIMEOUT_S
        int "Task watchdog timeout used when diag initialises the WDT itself (s)"
        default 5
        range 1 60
        depends on ESP_TASK_WDT_EN && !ESP_TASK_WDT_INIT
        help
            When the system does not initialise the task watchdog at boot
            (ESP_TASK_WDT_INIT off), diag_task_register() initialises it on first use
            with this timeout. When ESP_TASK_WDT_INIT is on, the system's
            ESP_TASK_WDT_TIMEOUT_S applies and this symbol is hidden.

endmenu
